  "fullDescription": "Procreate Brushes Christmas hat & Christmas tree, Christmas Tree Brushes, Christmas Tree Brush, Christmas Brushes, Christmas Brush, Christmas procreate, Tree Brushes, Tree Brush, Trees Brushes, Trees Brush, Tree procreate, Christmas Tree, Christmas hat, Christmas hat Brushes, Christmas hat Brush, Hat Brushes, Hat Brush, Hat procreate, procreate, Procreate brushes stamp, procreate brush stamp, procreate brushes, procreate brush, brushes stamp, brush stamp, procreate, addons procreate\n\nProcreate Brushes Christmas hat & Christmas tree. There are 60 individual stamps included in this procreate brush. These stamp brushes are great for creating digital and printable projects which are graphic design, stationery & printable, doodles, Instagram posts, blog posts, wall art, surface patterns, packaging, posters, business cards, illustrations, blog buttons, etc.\n\nYOU WILL RECEIVE:\n– 1 Zip of 2 files, which are:\n1) 1 brush set file with 60 stamps created in Procreate. There are 23 Christmas tree Brushes, 26 Christmas hat Brushes and 11 Christmas Elements Brushes.\n2) Bonus (Value 5 dollor) : You will receive Bonus folder of Sublimation Merry Christmas Set2 containing 10 Merry Christmas in digital PNG files with transparent background for size 3,600 x 3,600 pixel (12” x12” approx.) in high resolution 300 DPI.\n\nHOW TO USE:\n– Download the brush set file and import it to your brushes in Procreate\n(Use with Procreate only!).\n– After install, choose a stamp and tap on your screen for your design.\n– You can scale / resize these stamp brushes, change opacity, color or set-ups.\n\nHOW TO INSTALL?\n– Open IPAD\n– Unzip file\n– Download brush set file and it will automatically import into procreate brush collection.\n\nIF NOT, DO THIS TUTORIAL:\n1. Download brush set file to folder on your iPad\n2. Open the folder and find downloaded brush set file\n3. Tap and hold with your finger or apple pencil\n4. Choose “Share” from the menu\n5. If the option “Open in Procreate” is missing, click on “More”\n6. Scroll and find the option “Open in Procreate” and click on it\n7. Open your project in Procreate and click on brush icon at the top right corner\n8. Find the new brush set in your Brush library\n\nIMPORTANT:\n– Use these brushes with Procreate App on IPAD only\n– These brushes DO NOT work in Photoshop or any other application.\n– This is a digital product. No physical product will be sent to you.\n\nBest Regard,\nTanvara T/.",
